# Domain State Machine Rules

- Model allowed status transitions as explicit maps, not scattered conditionals.
- Reject illegal transitions with domain errors and audit logging.
- Keep Pay-In and Pay-Out transition graphs separate.
- `Pay-In` and `Pay-Out` lifecycle behavior must match documented statuses.
- Timers and visual indicators must not silently auto-cancel unless spec explicitly requires it.
- Changes to status logic must include transition tests (happy path + invalid path).
- Any new status requires: migration/enum update, webhook compatibility review, and docs update.
